  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cbc795acf92c1fb48bae236e4ba4d39f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q03_Extrinsic_NType
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PNJunctionLab.AssessmentQuestion
  questionId: q03_ntype
  topic: 1
  topicTag: 2. Extrinsic Doping (N & P)
  shortSummaryLabel: N-Type Charge Neutrality
  promptText: Doping Silicon with Group V Phosphorus (P) at ND = 1e16 cm^-3 creates N-type Silicon. Which statement is true at room temperature?
  options:
  - The crystal holds net negative charge and Fermi level EF drops toward Ev
  - The crystal stays neutral (mobile e- balance fixed + donor ions) and EF shifts toward Ec
  - Holes become the majority carriers with p ~ ND
  - Donor energy level ED lies 0.045 eV above the valence band Ev
  correctIndex: 1
  explanation: Pentavalent donors (P, As, Sb) contribute a free electron (~0.045 eV below Ec) and leave a fixed + donor ion locked in the crystal, keeping total charge neutral while shifting EF up toward Ec.
  recommendedStation: Stations 2 & 3
